  "summary": "Renames formatPrice to formatMoney in src/money.ts and makes it format through Intl.NumberFormat with a currency argument. invoiceLines now passes a currency that defaults to USD.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "file_path": "src/money.ts",
      "line_number": 3,
      "line_end": 4,
      "title": "Removed export still imported by cart.ts",
      "description": "The change renames formatPrice to formatMoney and leaves no formatPrice export behind. src/cart.ts line 1 still imports formatPrice, and src/cart.ts line 8 still calls it. The TypeScript compiler rejects cart.ts, so the build fails. A bundler without type checks would ship a cart total that throws at runtime. Update src/cart.ts to call formatMoney with a currency. Another option is to keep formatPrice as a wrapper that calls formatMoney with USD.",
      "suggested_change": "export function formatMoney(cents: number, currency: string): string {\n  return new Intl.NumberFormat(\"en-US\", { style: \"currency\", currency }).format(cents / 100);\n}\n\nexport function formatPrice(cents: number): string {\n  return formatMoney(cents, \"USD\");\n}",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "The change renames formatPrice to formatMoney and leaves no formatPrice export behind. src/cart.ts line 1 still imports formatPrice, and src/cart.ts line 8 still calls it.",
      "consequence": "The TypeScript compiler rejects cart.ts, so the build fails. A bundler without type checks would ship a cart total that throws at runtime.",
      "fix": "Update src/cart.ts to call formatMoney with a currency. Another option is to keep formatPrice as a wrapper that calls formatMoney with USD."
    }
  ],
